worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_arithmetic_and_numeric_lists.js"
  ceiling 763
  rationale "The arithmetic handler with clock and compound-money formatting, link-native synthesis arithmetic and the numeric-list operations. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 810 to 812 for server parity (R1013): tryArithmetic records the calculator events `try_arithmetic` logs in Rust (`solverEvents`), which the JavaScript server projects into the native thinking trace. Lowered to 795 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the compounding-frequency labels left compoundLabel for the policy compound_interest block of data/seed/handler-rules.lino. Lowered to 758 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the numeric-list intros and result labels became seeded numeric_list_* responses read through NUMERIC_LIST_LOCALIZATION. Ceiling moved 758 to 761 for PR #1188 dogfooding (round 5): extractPythonFunctionName also reads a signature that a seeded program_synthesis_subject word names in any language (функцию both(a, b), 函数 both(a, b)), as the native inline_function_signature already does, so a non-English module-function request is synthesized. Ceiling moved 761 to 763 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds."
